__pycache__/
*.pyc
.edgeprof/

# Visual Studio's local cache, if anyone opens the folder there.
.vs/

# The Output folder IS committed on purpose -- a figure viewable on GitHub
# beside the code and the log entry that produced it is the point of it. Only
# the transcoded video scratch is not worth carrying.
Output/**/_videocache/

# Derived: a roll-up of everything in GUI_logs, regenerated on every boot.
# Tracking it would mean a merge conflict on literally every pull, over a file
# anyone can rebuild in a second. Everything real lives in the per-machine
# records it is compiled from.
GUI_logs/.cache/
GUI_logs/index.json

# The Supabase secret key. Never committed -- tools/cloud_setup.py refuses to
# write it unless git is already ignoring this path. If one does get pushed,
# rotate it in the Supabase dashboard; that is the only real fix.
GUI_logs/.cloud.json

# Who this machine is on the VACC: netid, key path, slurm account. Not a
# secret -- with key authentication the private key never leaves ~/.ssh and
# Jarvis never reads it -- but a netid is somebody's name, and where the
# cluster is and what it mounts are lab-wide facts that live in the tracked
# vacc.json instead. tools/vacc_setup.py refuses to write this unless git is
# already ignoring it.
GUI_logs/.vacc.json

# The browsable copy of the Event Bank. Derived from GUI_logs/event_bank (and
# from Supabase), regenerated whenever the bank changes, and deterministic --
# so it is safe to delete and pointless to track. Committing it would mean two
# machines with different halves of the bank taking turns adding and deleting
# each other's CSVs on every push.
Data Bank/

# The by-product lane. Harness screenshots, debug reports, the figure a test
# rendered to prove that rendering works -- real output of real runs, and
# nobody will ever cite one.
#
# They used to land in Results/ beside the figures. Of 197 files there, about
# 120 were this: forty-five "rebuild harness" PNGs, forty-nine debug reports,
# thirty "arrow harness" exports of which twenty-three were byte-identical to
# each other. A folder that is five percent results is not a folder anybody
# reads, and every one of them was committed.
#
# Still written and still findable -- `save_output(lane="scratch")` puts them
# here, the catalogue skips the folder, and git no longer carries them.
Results/_scratch/
